# Who must review what. The ruleset on main requires a code-owner review (docs/operations/LAUNCH.md).
# `@openmasonry` is a user account (the founding Master's project account), not a team. After the
# Founder's Sunset this file is changed, by a reviewed pull request, to list the witness operators' team.
#
# Everything needs a code-owner review except new ledger entries (and their anchors and reasons),
# which the judge alone admits.
# Later lines take precedence over earlier ones.

*                  @openmasonry

/canon/            @openmasonry
/CONSTITUTION.md   @openmasonry
/src/              @openmasonry
/bin/              @openmasonry
/scripts/          @openmasonry
/node/             @openmasonry
/.github/          @openmasonry
/skills/           @openmasonry
/AGENTS.md         @openmasonry
/CLAUDE.md         @openmasonry
/llms.txt          @openmasonry
/.claude/          @openmasonry
/.agents/          @openmasonry
/engines/          @openmasonry
/docs/             @openmasonry
/wiki/             @openmasonry

# canon/history/ holds every degree table the ledger ever pinned, as byte copies named by their sha256:
# replay reads each of them, so it has an owner (the judge also refuses any change there but an
# addition, and `verify --tree` requires every pinned table). Archive the genesis table by an ordinary
# reviewed PR before the genesis (docs/operations/LAUNCH.md), so the genesis PR holds entry 000000 alone.
/canon/history/    @openmasonry

# No owner: ledger PRs need no code-owner review.
# The judge refuses any ledger PR that changes anything else, and the admit job enables auto-merge
# once the judge passes. ledger/anchors/ holds the witness's OpenTimestamps proofs, which travel with
# its checkpoint entries. ledger/reasons/ holds the public reasons of corrections, each named after
# its own sha256, which travel with the correction entries that pin them (verify --tree checks them).
# A directory pattern covers everything below it: /ledger/entries/ covers every shard (ledger/entries/NNNN/).
/ledger/entries/
/ledger/anchors/
/ledger/reasons/
